EntMod_i386.so -- EntMod (reconstructed), a Metamod plugin for The Specialists on H9XASH.

NOT a patch of an upstream binary. The original EntMod ("Ent Mod v4", Drunken_F00l / remortal,
adminop.net) was abandoned with no source; it was reverse-engineered from the shipped EntMod_MM.dll /
EntMod_i386.so into clean, recompilable C++ at EntMod4/src/EntMod4/ (faithful original) +
EntMod4/src/h9/ (HAVOC9 additions). Metamod-only (the standalone game-DLL shim + entity trampolines
were dropped; H9XASH runs Metamod-R).

Build:
  Windows:  MSBuild EntMod4/src/EntMod4/msvc/EntMod.vcxproj /p:Configuration=Release;Platform=Win32;PlatformToolset=v143  -> EntMod4/dist/EntMod_MM.dll
  Linux:    make -C EntMod4/src/EntMod4  -> EntMod_i386.so

HAVOC9 additions (src/h9): DF_admins admin parity (accept the h9_clientid Xash id as well as the
engine auth id / SteamID; _entpass still required); the entmod / entmod_maps gate -- the tools turn
ON when the map name contains "entmap" (the entmod-map naming convention), the map is one of the
";"-separated names in the entmod_maps cvar, or the operator set "entmod 1"; inert otherwise. While
active the server de-ranks (no career XP / ELO) via the h9_compete.sma / h9_presence.sma entmod_map()
gate. The on/off decision and the exact map name are printed to the server console each map
("[EntMod] map '<name>' -> tools ON/off") so activation can be confirmed in-game.
